MPTDC fast-domain feasibility audit
===================================
Generated: 2026-06-02 10:50:51 CEST

Purpose
-------
Desk-check the physical plausibility of treating oscillator-domain
standard-cell registers as ordinary single-cycle synchronous logic.

Timing equation
---------------
A same-clock register-to-register path must satisfy:
  Tclk >= Tcq_launch + Tcomb + Tsetup_capture + uncertainty - useful_skew

Current targets
---------------
  clk_osc_fast period: 1.567 ns
  clk_osc_slow period: 1.667 ns
  oscillator setup uncertainty: 0.050 ns

Review rule
-----------
If reported library Tcq plus setup and uncertainty approaches or
exceeds the target oscillator period before combinational delay, RTL
pipeline slicing cannot close the path. The architecture must either
move the affected logic to a slower clock, use custom/analog latch
macros with a real Liberty contract, or explicitly classify the path
as measurement fabric rather than ordinary synthesized reg-to-reg logic.

Evidence to inspect
-------------------
  timing_pd_capture_hotspots.rpt
  timing_osc_counter_hotspots.rpt
  timing_osc_fast_full_clock.rpt
  timing_meas_ctrl_hotspots.rpt
  timing_context_bank_hotspots.rpt
  Innovus preCTS/postRoute full_clock timing reports
